{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Her name shall no longer be called Sarai.</b> For every yod characterizes the male, and we find this expression for a male, as it is written (Judges 5:15) וְשָׂרַי בְּיִשָּׂשכָר — because she was barren like males who do not give birth. But now a heh was given to her in place of the yod, for every heh characterizes the female, to indicate that from now on she would be a female who gives birth. And so that the yod not have a grievance, as it were, saying that it was uprooted from the Torah and lost half its number, therefore He added the heh to Abraham as well, granting him dominion over a multitude of nations and over the five organ-heads. And according to the masters of Kabbalah, the heh possesses the power of procreation, as it is written (Genesis 47:23) ״הֵא לָכֶם זֶרַע״, and as she said (Genesis 30:2) ״הֲתַחַת אֱלֹהִים אָנֹכִי״ etc. And this is the reason for the two hehs of Bilhah. Therefore two hehs were given here — one for Abraham and one for Sarah. And the heh was taken from Sarah for Abraham, to indicate that the merit of Sarah caused them this procreation — just as she said (Genesis 30:3) ״וְאִבָּנֶה גַם אָנֹכִי מִמֶּנָּה״ — by the merit that she brought her rival into her house. And if so, the merit of Sarah caused Abraham to beget children. Another matter: therefore the heh was given to them, for with a heh HaShem created the world, and 'not for a void did He create it, but to be inhabited He formed it' (Isaiah 45:18); therefore the heh would be the cause of their procreations for the purpose of settling the world. And it is possible that what is said (Genesis 12:2) ״וַאֲגַדְּלָה שְׁמֶךָ״ — with the addition of the heh — hints that He would add a heh to his name, and by means of this cause ״אֶעֶשְׂךָ לְגוֹי גָּדוֹל״."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "The Kli Yakar alludes to the midrashic tradition (Bereishit Rabbah 47) that the yod removed from Sarai's name complained to HaShem until He placed it into the name of Joshua (Yehoshua); the phrase 'half its number' refers to the numerical values: yod = 10, heh = 5. The reference to 'five organ-heads' (חמשה ראשי אברים) concerns the five-letter divine name potential in Abraham's augmented name, per kabbalistic teaching."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:28:30.459067649Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}